Since $\quad U_E \times c=I=$ Intensity
<br/><br/>$$
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{1}{2} \varepsilon_0 E^2 \times c=I=\frac{P}{4 \pi R^2}=\frac{3 / 100 \times P}{4 \pi R^2} \\\\
E & =\sqrt{\frac{6 P}{\varepsilon_0 \times c \times 100 \times 4 \pi R^2}} \\\\
& =\sqrt{\frac{6 \times 100}{8.85 \times 10^{-12} \times 3 \times 10^8 \times 100 \times 4 \pi \times(5)^2}} \\\\
& =2.68 \mathrm{~V} / \mathrm{m}
\end{aligned}
$$
